n"},"level":"2","description":{"zh":"经过华丽处理的贤士冠，多为朝中身居要职之人佩戴。","en":"An ornately finished scholar's crown, worn by those holding high court positions."},"mp":"1500","evade":"8","price":"9500","slot":{"zh":"头盔","en":"Helmet"}}],"family":{"children":{"label":{"zh":"子女","en":"Children"},"people":[{"id":"WJ1050215","code":"100"}]},"family":{"label":{"zh":"亲属","en":"Relatives"},"people":[{"id":"WJ1050115","code":"100"}]}},"clans":[{"id":"GI113415","name":{"zh":"金海金氏","en":"The Kim clan of Gimhae"},"years":["0","999"],"desc":{"zh":"也称伽倻金氏，出自弁韩部落。始祖金首露于建立伽倻（又称加耶、伽耶），是以金官伽倻为中心的城邦联盟。伽倻以铁器制造与贸易闻名，为半岛南部重要政权，与三国时期完全重叠。作为连接半岛与外部世界的铁器贸易中心，伽倻在半岛政治格局中扮演了重要角色。其王族“金海金氏”后世繁盛，有约六百万后裔，为韩国第一大宗族。","en":"Also known as the Gaya Kim clan, originating from the Byeonhan tribes. The founding ancestor King Suro established Gaya (also written as Gayan or Kaya), a confederacy of city-states centered on Geumgwan Gaya. Gaya was renowned for iron Crafting and trade, serving as a vital power in the southern Korean Peninsula whose existence coincided fully with the Three Kingdoms period. As an iron trade hub linking the peninsula with the outside world, Gaya played a crucial role in regional politics. Its royal lineage, the Gimhae Kim clan, flourished in later eras with roughly six million descendants, making it the largest clan in Korea."},"talent":{"military":"6","commerce":"5","politics":"7"}}],"friendGroups":[],"body":{"name":"金首露","height":"平均","shape":"较瘦"},"honorifics":[],"selfAddress":[],"specialNames":[],"vip":{"isVIP":0,"from":"0","to":"0"},"marriage":{"aiMarriageAge":"25","startPregnantAge":"0"},"scenarios":[{"story":{"id":"S10802","name":{"zh":"黄巾起义","en":"Yellow Turban Rebellion"},"year":"184","month":"3"},"faction":null,"city":"CS1068","noRecruit":false,"reject":null,"state":"2","role":0,"stats":[60,62,83,87,85,88],"title":1,"rank":"1","loyalty":"100","reputation":"0","equipment":{"weapon":"WP1007102","armor":"WP1015005","helmet":"WP1028205"},"couple":[]},{"story":{"id":"S10215","name":{"